From afc02f264f1f089c3ac47f8b8c5e17d456c99202 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:29:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Bindings: layout of the managers, Fortran tangent operator,
 numpy strides

- C and Fortran: getter of the layout of a material data manager.
- Fortran: material_data_manager_get_tangent_operator refuses the
  component by component layout, as the other accessors, and its first
  extent (size of the thermodynamic forces) is now set (it was never set).
- Python: an array of values given by a strided numpy array (for instance
  `a[::2]`) is refused instead of being read as contiguous.
- tests: invalid layout refused by the C bindings, layout of the managers,
  tangent operator in both layouts in Fortran, strides of the
  thermodynamic forces and of the tangent operator in Python, strided
  arrays refused.
---
 .../MGIS/Behaviour/MaterialDataManager.h      |  9 ++++++-
 bindings/c/src/MaterialDataManager.cxx        | 13 +++++++++
 bindings/c/tests/LayoutTest-c.c               |  8 ++++++
 bindings/fortran/src/mgis_behaviour.f90       | 27 +++++++++++++++++++
 bindings/fortran/tests/LayoutTest-f.f90       | 22 +++++++++++++++
 bindings/python/tests/LayoutTest.py           | 14 ++++++++++
 6 files changed, 92 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

